92db1a4-5afb-55cc-a7cc-c2f2533a1438" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121268/selection/c50cc7102ba0a56f38ebde7e5abd53eea4e34a7145d1711542f993a0025031b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-121268/selection/5f766e451418bdec60002d17d612b0384cbfe5ba1aa00e19b1e84898eb3593c1" "q-121268/selection/808b4ef6001cdcc48fd573b2adebbaecaef25221e6e91df61ec73d8b7ac32f81" "q-121268/selection/7f4cad89925875cba0a6e630aafdc517a416b34a4f9e1f4e49466342ad65b799" "q-121268/selection/c50cc7102ba0a56f38ebde7e5abd53eea4e34a7145d1711542f993a0025031b1" "q-121268/selection/6ad89013794d7ee6fefa737574aa6572f0fb155a76ad0eb71e2a75f03ef6e4fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121268" :question/id #uuid "89d7879e-efea-5b0c-9087-4e16cff8d558" :question/math-academy-id "q-121268" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y-2).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/2ae1b749a56deaef05254ff376acbd44885337b06b49473cb9b19b4fa57f6c84.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/6434bee1a3dc38292675749072f046d4af6239ce6a8f71f102a9b29637679da4.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-1)$ | $(y-2)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(0,3)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(2,3)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(0,1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)>0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/17551c745895bac085fc289f9ff0f26531bc518891815e252885fd75d81a0af0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121268/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection/6ec7f55390e84a805c2f4b28c93f893967d5f7a64eeb901750d34dda29cf16f4" :answer/id #uuid "4202c560-65d8-5a16-b7b8-d406d803752a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" :answer/id #uuid "f3c4fff8-c863-5411-aefa-d995f8ca046a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054" :answer/id #uuid "ce6b38c9-84cb-5618-875d-54dba929f081" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" :answer/id #uuid "ddd98aa4-a892-5099-ba7e-e6ee0c0ca112" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309" :answer/id #uuid "fa6c4794-75ed-59a5-82d8-9c2ff6d361be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1face21b-2b63-54e6-9b37-962321d8d5c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121278/selection/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309" :answer-field/choices ["q-121278/selection/6ec7f55390e84a805c2f4b28c93f893967d5f7a64eeb901750d34dda29cf16f4" "q-121278/selection/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" "q-121278/selection/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054" "q-121278/selection/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" "q-121278/selection/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121278" :question/id #uuid "9195bf5b-e185-53ad-970f-942b816b9aec" :question/math-academy-id "q-121278" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=(x+1)(2-y).$ What are the missing entries in the sign table of $f(x,y),$ shown below?\n\n| $y>2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-1$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/d5d7c89d619aa13d7fea8bc1260a08cb8678fb260e4431508c5f4c8c53e7ba5e.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/6cce64627f21f6cc17efc789614a0bd582ded827a0938f01c9b756e0cb461862.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+1)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(0,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(0,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/c24cc3ab0812bfae6834ff8c3a68668c3925f6e39e29a453ea6bc27fbc9f6c74.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the table as follows:\n\n| $y>2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection/6ae00d880ea98d29959c548478acf097331201953111a5701291faa6dd4ea6ce" :answer/id #uuid "26a986b6-012e-5094-a812-6714e976e5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/f12e4490704485f3b05921fe9e25b21bc04aa389995ec2e4580593f63883e47c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection/087a6afddd10bb3b177cfca9490a417bc7245b0f58ac1191ec323390a61f8e6d" :answer/id #uuid "c731b5cb-a6b0-5a00-8688-55d70711591f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/97e1785d876935df14a9d7cea236f536c90b68fa1bad2bf8418569c80e56ba12.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection/9ac1ad6806078faf587991ba4592dbabd4c7bd4744baff1ddbc3360f365fd533" :answer/id #uuid "89dce387-0459-545e-9037-a100dad3d10c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/f0614c91d93dc23135aad96e908562cfe1f6726f1c2b641f0ee55952deb4625b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection/769f9f95baadd026bc436416d685c9376abf2b5114202faf43038c9174830095" :answer/id #uuid "12a669e5-6040-56a5-890c-55593b954e73" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/8a9becf0529b2896627d44fef11066d684c50479e62166ccc777a6250cd24033.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection/08bf129e9e3f990038acfa50fff7a01cd4a0ed77666964b26980d03980264d2b" :answer/id #uuid "34e8a91c-2fbe-5b32-bd99-a19b88fdaa7f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/0ba31669fe6eb9d3eadd9423de52ea1042300fdc098cb3e9bd8081ed458c0d07.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce98d6f6-0564-515b-b6de-c7adfea9fc7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149547/selection/087a6afddd10bb3b177cfca9490a417bc7245b0f58ac1191ec323390a61f8e6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-149547/selection/6ae00d880ea98d29959c548478acf097331201953111a5701291faa6dd4ea6ce" "q-149547/selection/087a6afddd10bb3b177cfca9490a417bc7245b0f58ac1191ec323390a61f8e6d" "q-149547/selection/9ac1ad6806078faf587991ba4592dbabd4c7bd4744baff1ddbc3360f365fd533" "q-149547/selection/769f9f95baadd026bc436416d685c9376abf2b5114202faf43038c9174830095" "q-149547/selection/08bf129e9e3f990038acfa50fff7a01cd4a0ed77666964b26980d03980264d2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149547" :question/id #uuid "5272563d-3782-5aa6-b37c-de65aac06d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-149547" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(x+2){y}^{3}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-2$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/975b596621dab7d455b09d75b1c8d2b9fd73e75cd2169ec40aadda48673f6883.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/9466a3fbf682ce967cda2294cfb61d5fa40b4f7c91686cfc8653cb4c1ffb4e97.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+2)$ | ${y}^{3}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-3,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-3,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/b8e5807115c13aa842364a174058d1081bd84eba10dce13390da93832a1aeb54.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149547/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149550/selection/d0f1f246fc3a2375759bbc71a2c2fa4835183c574acc18331c4708f69bdb5e45" :answer/id #uuid "be469f9c-054d-55d1-b764-7ba7fd34b7c4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/7c1521cfad08f4c1cc4a699066ec5dc84fd635c2f1d39f71dca5a8ba86533887.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149550/selection/8ce3c4689aa432844203f43ca47578307fd5887c15deb763175f73dcc218ea65" :answer/id #uuid "39bafa95-736b-5e31-ba87-57e44397aae8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/1cadc33591f95b5b66f50794e329768364708bb7f9de1e06d579ff1833be11d4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149550/selection/6d0220c351a5162ef646a078ee889f5d5192