Suppose that $f(x,y)=(3-x){y}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)<0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=3$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/e4d289aef282e076b062aab6d8f0f209396313e2c6403b2e27d1c0272ac90795.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/4cef3532a8e70098c030f2341800f06e9e54e4074126a0a97aecdf1f1c5185d0.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(3-x)$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(4,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(2,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(4,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)<0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/c9ed172c5746b1b0afd2d9b7b3bbb21245115df164bfb7e34f4f530887376e28.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149550/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149550"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-1/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer/id #uuid "6801b55f-6b3c-5b5a-b4aa-426ef1df51b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-1/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer/id #uuid "6b47fd2f-14a8-5532-95c1-d4cff81e403a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "+" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fab76f8-afff-5d98-99a2-61bc1232b7da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-326447/field-1/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer-field/choices ["q-326447/field-1/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" "q-326447/field-1/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-2/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer/id #uuid "572a8bbf-133c-58f6-905c-8d2209cc7cfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-2/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer/id #uuid "7d7c3510-600a-5662-982e-b3d814156854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "+" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f099285-833d-5037-b125-05d84699808a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-326447/field-2/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-326447/field-2/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" "q-326447/field-2/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-3/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer/id #uuid "affa9442-fb34-576d-b79e-5bf0452d918c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "+" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-3/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer/id #uuid "1e71a619-05b6-5795-9357-15b324ff59d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "db7713df-acaf-5d19-a163-b950bac063c1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-326447/field-3/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-326447/field-3/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" "q-326447/field-3/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-4/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer/id #uuid "322e9427-496a-5b75-ab6f-69621c7c0c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "+" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-4/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer/id #uuid "38412ded-eb16-516d-834a-3c7beab57b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b32d6df6-4ed5-5a0e-b54d-18f890d768ad" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-326447/field-4/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer-field/choices ["q-326447/field-4/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" "q-326447/field-4/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326447" :question/id #uuid "781a7b30-39ba-54da-b0a1-cd00e6093626" :question/math-academy-id "q-326447" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=(x-1)(2-y).$ Fill in the missing signs in the sign table of $f(x,y)$ shown below.\n\n| $y>2$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/4244ec01c3ca7ea666967abfea565c5674f8740033f365b138a9488899b2017a.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/4d115bf92aa8255a17ee6e658026570c683d1bc65fc342463d7e66f58d4df554.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-1)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(0,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(2,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(0,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/91e3506692c75397376f3addbcab0636bb817462eec529206ba3a62c84d901be.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-326447/field-1" "q-326447/field-2" "q-326447/field-3" "q-326447/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
